From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 16:32:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath10k: don't set DSSS/CCK in 40 MHz on 5 GHz

ath10k_get_ht_cap() sets IEEE80211_HT_CAP_DSSSCCK40 unconditionally:

	ht_cap.cap |= IEEE80211_HT_CAP_DSSSCCK40;

and ath10k_mac_setup_ht_vht_cap() then assigns the one resulting structure to
both the 2 GHz and the 5 GHz band. DSSS and CCK are 2.4 GHz modulations, so
"DSSS/CCK Mode in 40 MHz" says nothing in a 5 GHz association, and clients
that get this right do not set it there.

ath10k_get_ht_cap() has no band context to decide with, so clear the bit at
the point the 5 GHz band is populated and leave 2 GHz untouched:

	2 GHz  Capabilities: 0x19ef
	5 GHz  Capabilities: 0x09ef

No behaviour change is claimed beyond the advertisement itself. This was
found while chasing an AP that refused this client, but that refusal was a
reserved VHT channel width pair and is fixed separately; the AP accepted both
before and after this patch. It is worth fixing on its own terms.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
index 4afe880c4639..36bf43b7c2d5 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
@@ -5071,6 +5071,12 @@ static void ath10k_mac_setup_ht_vht_cap(struct ath10k *ar)
 	if (ar->phy_capability & WHAL_WLAN_11A_CAPABILITY) {
 		band = &ar->mac.sbands[NL80211_BAND_5GHZ];
 		band->ht_cap = ht_cap;
+		/* DSSS and CCK are 2.4 GHz modulations, so "DSSS/CCK Mode in
+		 * 40 MHz" is meaningless in a 5 GHz association.
+		 * ath10k_get_ht_cap() has no band context and sets it
+		 * unconditionally; clear it here, where the band is known.
+		 */
+		band->ht_cap.cap &= ~IEEE80211_HT_CAP_DSSSCCK40;
 		band->vht_cap = vht_cap;
 	}
 }
